The CPU checks confirmed three defects: zero-extent core shapes reach signed overflow, host allocation failure in the new drain path aborts the process, and `synchronize()` returns success when `cudaGetDevice` fails. The original None crashes and the ordinary nonzero overflow cases now produce clean refusals. I’m adding a controlled shutdown-race check and lead probes for the GPU-only paths.

